      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wormleysburg was named for its founder, John Wormley, and became an incorporated borough in May 1916.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wormleysburg%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Wormley settled on the West Shore in 1772 and later founded the town of Wormleysburg in 1815.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wormleysburgpa.org/history/wormleysburg_borough_history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The John Wormley House was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1976.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wormleysburg%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wormleysburg sits on the west bank of the Susquehanna River, directly across from the state capital of Harrisburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
